  "summary": "ACCEPT. Fresh read-only combined definition review iteration 5 ran the speckit-analyze prerequisite explicitly against feature 011 and independently reviewed the raw Story 12.2 record, specification/checklist, complete regenerated plan set and contracts, 52-task graph, Constitution, AGENTS.md, Ubiquitous Language, PRD and dated August authorities, Story 12.1 contracts, all prior raw definition verdicts, the accepted fifth-correction authorization, and relevant source/test seams. Semantic inventory found 43 unique Functional Requirements, nine unique Success Criteria, and 52 unique sequential task IDs with complete requirement and buildable-success-criterion coverage, no unresolved placeholders, no blocking ambiguity or duplication, no Constitution MUST conflict, and no material terminology drift. DR4-001 is closed: PreparedScanManifestEntry is a prepared-only principal whose key, manifest binding, File Code Unit ID/fingerprint, scores, reasons, and both ordinals are non-null; selected audits use its valid composite principal while historical CodeUnit prepared fields remain nullable non-key values requiring no backfill, and T040/T045/T050 cover EF model creation, PostgreSQL apply/rollback/reapply, legacy null-row readability, association rejection, independent reconstruction, atomicity, and replay. DR4-002 is closed: production-literal T049, migration T045, PostgreSQL atomicity/replay T050, workflow/security T048/T051, real-tool T046, and release T047 qualifications all physically precede the sole final T052 barrier; T052 explicitly depends on T031 and T045-T051, and nothing follows it. DR4-003 is closed: quickstart provenance identifies the accepted fifth-correction authorization and raw attempt-4 source. Earlier audit-preimage, prepared-context identity, safe-XML range ownership, exact replay, release-repeatability, production-literal, TDD, and verification-filter corrections remain preserved. Runtime and scope pins remain exact: Vulgata, CodeGraph @colbymchenry/codegraph@1.5.0, Java 21, and JDT LS jdt-language-server-1.61.0-202608141332 over StreamJsonRpc 2.25.29 stdio run on Windows; PostgreSQL 17 is the only required Docker service; CodeGraphContext is excluded. Story 12.3 Worker execution, navigate_code, dispatch/retry/lease policy, Documents, final Edges/Uncertainties, Cross-Repository Resolution, Pass 2, and Chat remain excluded. One nonblocking Medium task-ownership duplication between T048 and T051 should be normalized during implementation partitioning without changing accepted behavior or qualification ordering. git diff --check and the repository workflow validator passed apart from line-ending notices. No file, lifecycle state, index, commit, branch, or Git history was changed. Production implementation remains unauthorized pending the separate implementation-approval gate."
